## Accept nested page-object double-encoding in Ontology Generate completion

Context:
Ontology Generate → Complete failed live with
`output must contain a 'attributes' list` after ~37s. Relations had passed;
the attributes page from Claude under `response_format` json_schema came
back as a stringified *page object* inside the list field
(`{"attributes": "{\"attributes\": [...], \"has_more\": false}"}`). The
parser already unwrapped a stringified bare array, but not this nested
shape — same residual transport quirk documented for Sonnet endpoints.

Changes:

1. src/agents/agent_owl_generator/schemas.py
   `_require_list` now accepts one extra decode of a field string into
   either a list or a dict carrying that same key as a list (and promotes
   inner `has_more` when the outer object omitted it). Reject-only /
   single-decode policy unchanged for anything else.
2. tests/units/agents/test_owl_generator_schemas.py
   Added page-object double-encoding cases for attributes, relations, and
   axioms.

