## Accept grouped-by-kind axioms dict in Ontology Generate completion

Context:
Ontology Generate → Complete failed live with
`output must contain a 'axioms' list` (task 6432a73f, ~52s). Relations and
attributes substages had succeeded; only the axioms substage failed. The
axioms prompt enumerates three axiom kinds (subClassOf / disjointWith /
equivalentClass), so the endpoint intermittently returned the `axioms`
field as a dict whose values are lists grouped by kind
(`{"subClassOf": [...], "disjointWith": [...]}`) instead of a single
`axioms` list. `schemas._require_list` only tolerated the JSON-string
double-encoding quirk on `str` values; a plain dict value fell through to
the `output must contain a 'axioms' list` reject. The actual failing LLM
content was not recoverable (tracing logs token counts only; the in-memory
task store had `result: null`), so the fix is conservative and adds a
diagnostic log so the next residual quirk is self-diagnosing.

Changes:

1. src/agents/agent_owl_generator/schemas.py
   New `_dict_to_list(obj, key, data)` helper coerces a dict field value
   into a list for two recognised shapes: page-object re-wrap
   (`{"<key>": [...], "has_more": false}` — use the inner list, promote
   `has_more`) and grouped-by-kind (`{"subClassOf": [...], ...}` — flatten
   all list values into one list, only when every non-`has_more` value is a
   list). `_require_list` now applies this coercion to both the
   string-decoded result and a plain dict value; anything else is returned
   unchanged and rejected. Added a diagnostic `logger.info` on final reject
   (top-level keys + value type) so the next failure is diagnosable from the
   server log. A single axiom object (dict with non-list values) is NOT
   auto-wrapped — too speculative; the diagnostic log will reveal if that is
   the actual shape. Module docstring note updated for the new shape.
2. tests/units/agents/test_owl_generator_schemas.py
   Added grouped-by-kind dict cases for axioms (flatten + `has_more`
   promotion), the same shape as a JSON-encoded string, relations and
   attributes grouped dicts, plain-dict page-rewrap, and a non-grouped dict
   still rejected.
3. tests/eval/staged_contract.py
   New `_c_accepts_grouped_axioms_dict` check: scripts `infer_axioms` with
   a grouped-dict payload built from the example's own `input.draft`,
   asserts success + parsed axiom kinds; registered in `_CHECKS`.
4. tests/eval/datasets/agent_owl_generator/baseline.jsonl
   New staged row `staged-grouped-axioms-001` (stage `complete_axioms`,
   `cls-Customer-a1` anchor + `cand-6` candidate, constraint kind
   `accepts_grouped_axioms_dict`).
5. tests/eval/datasets/agent_owl_generator/regression.jsonl
   New regression row `regression-axioms-grouped-dict-004` documenting the
   live failure, root cause, and fix coverage.
6. tests/eval/run_agent_owl_generator.py
   Bumped `_MIN_STAGED_EXAMPLES` 43 -> 44 (45 staged rows now, 1-buffer);
   added `accepts_grouped_axioms_dict` to `_REQUIRED_STAGED_CONSTRAINT_KINDS`.

AI-feature gate note: this is a parser bug fix under `src/agents/**`, gated
by `.cursor/12-ai-feature-lifecycle.mdc`. The deterministic staged contract
(CI gate G2) passes offline (`python tests/eval/run_agent_owl_generator.py`,
no `--live`). A live MLflow eval run URI is required in the PR body when this
goes to PR but cannot be produced from this environment (no live endpoint
access).

